1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,134
60% winners vs 35% winners. Guess who's losing.

2
00:00:04,135 --> 00:00:07,868
Mostly Wrong loses 13 of 20. Ouch.

3
00:00:07,869 --> 00:00:11,199
And still finishes $1,200 ahead. Huh.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,720
Luck? We ran both 1,000 times.

5
00:00:14,721 --> 00:00:18,666
Same coin flips. Only the rules differ.

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:22,399
Mostly Right, 1,000 times. Median: −20%.

7
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:26,132
Only 8% of runs end up.

8
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:30,105
Mostly Wrong, same flips. Median: +40%.

9
00:00:30,106 --> 00:00:33,599
97% of runs end up.

10
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,332
Right loses $20 a trade. Wrong makes $40.

11
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:41,066
How often you win is half of it.

12
00:00:41,067 --> 00:00:44,608
Mostly Wrong's usual worst streak: 9 losses.

13
00:00:44,609 --> 00:00:48,532
In a row. Feels awful. Plan for it.

14
00:00:48,533 --> 00:00:52,668
Being right feels great. It doesn't pay rent.

15
00:00:52,669 --> 00:00:55,999
Count the dollars, not the wins.

16
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,549
Lore 002. Next: Lore 003, R: the only unit a trader needs
